# Applies to v3/deploy/Dockerfile regardless of build context root (BuildKit
# convention: `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`, relative to the context
# root). Admits exactly what the Dockerfile's COPY lines read — v2 code
# (the repo root outside `v3/`), `v3/.venv`, `v3/site/docs/node_modules`
# and every other tree stay out of the context. A bare `!v3` used to
# re-include the whole of `v3/` (issue #400), which made the lines below it
# redundant and shipped a local checkout's venv and node_modules into every
# build context. server/tests/deploy/test_dockerignore.py keeps this list
# and the Dockerfile's COPY sources in step.
*
!v3/pyproject.toml
!v3/uv.lock
!v3/server
!v3/web
!v3/clients
!v3/deploy
# server/pyproject.toml's dev group names the SDK through a `../sdk` path
# source; uv resolves the lockfile's sources even with --no-dev, so the
# (small) SDK tree rides along. Its own venv does not.
!v3/sdk

v3/server/.venv
v3/server/tests
v3/sdk/.venv
v3/server/**/__pycache__
v3/server/**/*.pyc
v3/server/.pytest_cache
v3/server/.mypy_cache
v3/server/.ruff_cache
v3/web/node_modules
v3/web/dist
v3/web/.vite
v3/deploy/pi-image/out
.git
